posts.body:
So, update on this! With the help of a friend I've figured out exactly how the enemy layering is handled in battle (even if I don't know how it's handled in the rpg maker viewer)
pixi.js, I think? Its battler layering relies on the
createEnemies
function found in
rpg_sprites.js.
And in
createEnemies
, it sorts the sprites using
compareEnemySprite
, which is the function just beneath it, which is as follows:
Code:
Spriteset_Battle.prototype.compareEnemySprite = function(a, b) {
    if (a.y !== b.y) {
        return a.y - b.y;
    } else {
        return b.spriteId - a.spriteId;
    }
};
This is why it appears that they'd be sorted by Id, when in reality they're sorted by y value, and then Id when the y values are the same.
So to change the ordering, I need to hijack that function in a plugin and stuff it full of my own code, wherein I can force it to compare notetags. I just finished a really ugly looking plugin myself that works as intended, and might post something when it looks better.
